## 4. Modelo de dados e contrato de evento

```sql
CREATE TABLE spins (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, spin_id TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  number INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK(number BETWEEN 0 AND 36),
  ts INTEGER NOT NULL, source TEXT NOT NULL,   -- ws | mo | ocr
  received_at INTEGER NOT NULL, latency_ms INTEGER
);
CREATE TABLE intents (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, spin_id TEXT NOT NULL, strategy_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  ladder_step INTEGER, stake_total_cents INTEGER, ev_cents INTEGER,
  confidence REAL, created_at INTEGER, decision TEXT  -- placed | skipped | aborted
);
CREATE TABLE fills (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, intent_id INTEGER REFERENCES intents(id),
  cover TEXT, stake_cents INTEGER, acked INTEGER, confirmed_at INTEGER
);
CREATE TABLE ladder_state (
  strategy_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, step INTEGER, loss_cents INTEGER, reset_at INTEGER
);
```

`intents` + `fills` existem porque **o bot precisa sobreviver a crash no meio do clique**. No boot: qualquer intent sem `fills` confirmados vira `orphan` e é reconciliada contra o extrato antes de qualquer nova entrada.

